--- type — runtime type introspection interface for the handl platform.
---
--- This .hnl declares the capability surface for the `type` library plugin
--- (id `lib.type`, display name `lib-type`). The plugin is a façade for the
--- Handl pure type system (re-exporting `handl-plugin-typecheck-nbe` and
--- `handl-kit-type-schema-json`), and also documents the runtime type
--- introspection ops that are registered by the `typeof` module in
--- `plugin-lib-utils`.
---
--- ## Runtime type introspection (typeof module)
---
--- The runtime module is named `typeof` (not `type`) because `type` became a
--- keyword in handl v0.1 (ADR-0074). The functions below are registered by
--- `TypeModule` in `plugin-lib-utils` and are callable as
--- `typeof.type_of(v)`, `typeof.is(v, kind)`, etc. in handl expressions.
---
--- typeof.type_of — return the type name of a value ("str", "num", "bool",
--- "null", "arr", "obj").
--- typeof.typeof — alias of type_of.
--- typeof.to_string — coerce a value to a string.
--- typeof.to_number — coerce a value to a number.
--- typeof.to_bool — coerce a value to a boolean.
--- typeof.identity — return the value unchanged.
--- typeof.default — return the value or a default if null.
--- typeof.coalesce — return the first non-null value among arguments.
--- typeof.is — test whether a value is of a given kind.
--- typeof.must — assert a value is of a given kind (error on mismatch).
--- typeof.may — test whether a value may be of a given kind.
--- typeof.not — test whether a value is not of a given kind.
--- typeof.when — conditional type guard returning the value or null.
---
--- ## Type tags
---
--- typeof.string — type tag for strings ("string").
--- typeof.str — short type tag for strings ("str").
--- typeof.number — type tag for numbers ("number").
--- typeof.num — short type tag for numbers ("num").
--- typeof.bool — type tag for booleans ("bool").
--- typeof.null — type tag for null ("null").
--- typeof.array — type tag for arrays ("array").
--- typeof.arr — short type tag for arrays ("arr").
--- typeof.object — type tag for objects ("object").
--- typeof.obj — short type tag for objects ("obj").
--- typeof.any — universal type tag (matches anything).
--- typeof.unknown — unknown type tag.
---
--- ## Typecheck engine (Rust façade)
---
--- The typecheck engine itself (NbE-based type synthesis, JSON Schema
--- interpretation) is implemented in Rust and re-exported by this crate.
--- It is not declared as `op`/`handl` here because it operates at the
--- compile-time/inference layer, not the eval-time dispatch layer.
cap "type.type_of"
cap "type.typeof"
cap "type.to_string"
cap "type.to_number"
cap "type.to_bool"
cap "type.identity"
cap "type.default"
cap "type.coalesce"
cap "type.is"
cap "type.must"
cap "type.may"
cap "type.not"
cap "type.when"
op "type.type_of" : Value -> String
  guarantee: IsString(output)
op "type.typeof" : Value -> String
  guarantee: IsString(output)
op "type.to_string" : Value -> String
  guarantee: IsString(output)
op "type.to_number" : Value -> Number
  guarantee: True
op "type.to_bool" : Value -> Bool
  guarantee: True
op "type.identity" : Value -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "type.default" : (Value, Value) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "type.coalesce" : Value -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "type.is" : (Value, String) -> Bool
  guarantee: True
op "type.must" : (Value, String) -> Value
  guarantee: True
op "type.may" : (Value, String) -> Bool
  guarantee: True
op "type.not" : (Value, String) -> Bool
  guarantee: True
op "type.when" : (Value, String) -> Value
  guarantee: True
